00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:10,080
 So we'll rule that one out.

167
00:14:10,080 --> 00:14:15,520
 The stylo-highway ligament runs from the styloid process to the hyroid bone, actually doesn't

168
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,800
 attach to the mandible at all.

169
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:22,960
 And it's calcified and symptomatic in eagle syndrome but doesn't limit movement of the

170
00:14:22,960 --> 00:14:23,960
 mandible.

171
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,840
 So we'll rule that one out as well.

172
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:29,240
 This phenomandibular ligament is an important one.

173
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:34,280
 It supports the mandible but it doesn't actually limit its movement.

174
00:14:34,280 --> 00:14:36,520
 So we can rule that one out as well.

175
00:14:36,520 --> 00:14:41,360
 And the stylo-mandibular ligament that goes from the styloid process to the angle of

176
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:44,600
 the mandible does limit movement.

177
00:14:44,600 --> 00:14:50,700
 It's the culprit for the finding why we don't just have the mandible protruding twelve, fifteen

