00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:18,880
 Alright so this is a nice straight forward muscle question and it's really just pure

185
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:20,760
 rote memorization.

186
00:15:20,760 --> 00:15:27,520
 The masseter muscle is one of those main muscles of mastication so it's absolutely fair game

187
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:30,600
 for the board exam.

188
00:15:30,600 --> 00:15:37,080
 The infrared temporal crest is the origin of the superior head of the lateral pterogoid

189
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:38,960
 muscle, not the masseter.

190
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:40,560
 So we can rule that one out.

191
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:47,840
 The lateral pterogoid plate is the origin for both pterogoids depending on the surface,

192
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:52,520
 ideal for medial pterogoid and lateral surface for lateral pterogoid muscle.

193
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:57,320
 So we can rule that one out as well and the mandibular angle is perhaps the most tempting

194
00:15:57,320 --> 00:16:03,640
 of these incorrect choices and it's the insertion of the masseter but we're looking for the

195
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:06,920
 origin so this is also incorrect.

196
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:15,600
 The correct answer here is zygomatic arch and that is where the masseter attaches.

197
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:22,960
 Alright question number 9, which of the following muscles is least likely to be activated during

198
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:24,560
