00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:39,680
 Alright so all of these muscles except for one is involved in smiling.

201
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:45,480
 The orbicularis oculi that surrounds both eyes is involved in squinting of the eye which

202
00:16:45,480 --> 00:16:50,920
 does happen during a duchine or candid enjoyment smile.

203
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,600
 So that is incorrect.

204
00:16:52,600 --> 00:16:54,560
 It does actually activate.

205
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:57,560
 The rhizoreous muscle is one of those smiling muscles as well.

206
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:04,480
 It pulls the corners of the lip laterally particularly during a grimace that's also incorrect.

207
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:09,920
 The zygomatic is major is perhaps the main smiling muscle that one is definitely incorrect

208
00:17:09,920 --> 00:17:16,680
 and the elevator angular ores elevates the corner of the mouth on both sides and so that's

209
00:17:16,680 --> 00:17:21,140
 definitely going to activate during a smile pulling up the corners of the lips so that

210
00:17:21,140 --> 00:17:23,560
 is also incorrect.

211
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:29,360
 And perhaps ironically the orbicularis ores that surrounds the mouth is actually the only

212
00:17:29,360 --> 00:17:33,160
 one that's activated not during a smile here.

213
00:17:33,160 --> 00:17:36,440
 It's only activated during puckering and frowning.

214
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:45,520
 So the orbicularis ores is maybe counter-intuitively the correct answer for this question.

215
00:17:45,520 --> 00:17:53,560
 It activates during a frown but not during a smile.

